---
description: Regression-test rules for numerical image-processing behavior.
globs: backend/tests/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

# Image-processing tests

- Use small synthetic arrays first; use real samples only when licensed and documented.
- Seed generated noise and state expected dtype/range/border behavior.
- Assert semantic invariants, dimensions, errors, and bounded numeric behavior.
- Avoid exact comparisons of lossy encoded files and float FFT output; justify tolerances.
- Every registry-backed operation needs a parameter-validation test and at least one operation-level test.
- Keep fixture files tiny; never add an undocumented or large binary asset.
